---
import Base from '~/layouts/Base.astro';
import Section from '~/components/Section.astro';
import { studio } from '~/config/site';

export const prerender = true;
---

<Base
  title={`Terms — ${studio.name}`}
  description={`The terms for using ${studio.name}'s website and commissioning work.`}
  canonicalPath="/terms"
>
  <Section id="terms" eyebrow="Legal" title="Terms" headingLevel={1}>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        The plain-language version. The binding version is the written contract
        signed before any project starts, and this page does not replace it.
      </p>

      <h2>About this site</h2>
      <p>
        This website is provided by {studio.name}. It is a portfolio and a way
        to make contact. You may browse it, link to it, and quote from it. You
        may not republish it as your own, scrape it at scale, or use it to send
        unsolicited commercial messages.
      </p>

      <h2>The work shown here</h2>
      <p>
        Projects displayed in the products section are our own work, work we
        built with a client, or experimental work. Where a project belongs to a
        client, its name and their team are credited on its page. Screenshots
        are of the public, live site as it appeared when the capture was taken;
        they are not representations of the current state of that site, and the
        linked product is not offered for sale through this page.
      </p>

      <h2>Availability</h2>
      <p>
        The site is provided as-is. Third-party project links may be broken,
        changed, or withdrawn by their owners; that is outside our control. We
        do not guarantee that any project linked from this site will remain
        available, though we do maintain the links we control.
      </p>

      <h2>Commissioning work</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing on this site is an offer, a quotation, or a contract. Work begins
        only after a written agreement covering scope, deliverables, price,
        payment schedule, IP transfer, and support terms has been signed by both
        sides. Any figure mentioned in conversation before that point is an
        estimate, not a commitment.
      </p>

      <h2>Before launch</h2>
      <p>
        The following must be reviewed by someone qualified in the studio's
        jurisdiction before the site goes live:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Governing law and jurisdiction clause.</li>
        <li>Limitation of liability and warranty disclaimers.</li>
        <li>Any consumer-cancellation rights that apply to the studio's location.</li>
        <li>Registered entity name and address, if required for business.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Base>
